write("docs/SONIC_DESIGN.md", '# Authentic tactile sound direction\n\nDrift uses sound as a material response to motion. It does not add music,\nambient beds, synthetic notification tones, or decorative hover noise.\n\nThe intended impression is a film editor handling physical media: cards\nsliding, a page turning, cloth catching, leather lifting, a book landing, a\nsmall latch engaging. The sounds are short enough to preserve narration and\nquiet enough that silence remains the dominant state.\n\n## Product rules\n\n1. **Picture remains primary.** Sound follows semantic carousel events; it does\n   not drive layout, timing, or export duration.\n2. **No surprise audio in the master.** New projects expose tactile preview but\n   exported effects are off by default. Projects migrated from schema v1 begin\n   with preview and export sound disabled.\n3. **No autoplay workaround.** Preview creates and resumes its `AudioContext`\n   only inside a trusted pointer or keyboard gesture. Enabling preview and the\n   explicit audition button are also valid unlock gestures.\n4. **No sound-only meaning.** Every cue accompanies a visible state change or\n   an existing status message.\n5. **No runtime third-party request.** Recordings are committed locally and\n   compiled inline. Export can run without the network.\n6. **One audio master.** Presenter speech and effects are mixed before AAC\n   encoding. Drift never emits competing audio tracks or silently drops one.\n7. **Deterministic export.** Cue time, sample choice, gain, playback rate, and\n   pan derive from saved project state and the pure carousel evaluator.\n8. **Restraint beats coverage.** There are no hover sounds, continuous scrubbing\n   loops, background ambience, or sound on every slider tick.\n\n## Semantic vocabulary\n\n| Cue | Meaning | Preview | MP4 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| passage | A logical slide crosses the viewing threshold | yes | yes |\n| grab | The user takes hold of the carousel | yes | no |\n| release | The user lets the carousel go | yes | no |\n| settle | Motion resolves into a resting state | yes | non-seamless endings |\n| control | A discrete editor command changes state | yes | no |\n| success | An existing operation completes successfully | yes | no |\n| failure | An existing operation fails visibly | yes | no |\n\nPreview passage cues are emitted by `CinematicCarousel` when its logical slot\nchanges. Export passage cues are generated by `buildSonicTimeline()` from the\nsame slide geometry, velocity, direction, asset count, seed, and duration used\nfor picture. Neither path scrapes rendered frames.\n\n## Material palettes\n\n### Studio\n\nPlaying-card slides, leather handling, paper, a small metal click, and soft\nsurface impacts. This is the restrained default: dry, close and editorial.\n\n### Cinema\n\nCard shoves, wood, metal latches, and slightly firmer impacts. It has more\nphysical weight without becoming a trailer-effects pack.\n\n### Paper\n\nPage turns, cloth, book movement, and soft landings. It is the least mechanical\npalette and suits quiet, tender, archival, or literary decks.\n\nEach semantic cue can draw from multiple authentic recordings. Variation is\ntherefore not just pitch modulation: deterministic sample selection prevents\nthe same page turn or card slide from repeating mechanically. Setting\nVariation to zero pins every cue to its first recording.\n\n## Preview engine\n\n`SonicEngine` owns a lazy Web Audio graph:\n\n- one master gain and one restrained compressor;\n- a maximum of eight simultaneous voices;\n- per-cue cooldowns;\n- density gating for passages;\n- separate motion and interface gain families;\n- stereo pan derived from horizontal direction;\n- short attack and release ramps to prevent clicks;\n- visibility suspension and complete teardown on unmount;\n- no decoding of a disabled migrated project\'s palette until the user opts in.\n\nThe engine is suppressed during export so preview feedback cannot leak into\nscreen capture, monitoring, or the exported master.\n\n## Export engine\n\n`buildSonicTimeline()` produces a deterministic list of passage and optional\nsettle events. `renderSonicSoundtrack()` renders that list through an exact\n48,000 Hz, two-channel `OfflineAudioContext`.\n\nAt export:\n\n- sound-only output becomes one AAC track;\n- presenter-only output remains one AAC track;\n- mixed output decodes presenter PCM and mixes the effects bed sample by sample\n  before one AAC encode;\n- the under-voice control scales effects when speech is present;\n- 50/60 fps audio-bearing output fails visibly under the existing codec gate;\n- cancellation is checked before decode, during sample submission, and after\n  offline rendering;\n- final output passes the existing readback and decoded-audio verification.\n\n## Sources and provenance\n\nAll recordings come from Kenney\'s **Casino Audio**, **RPG Audio**, and\n**Impact Sounds** packs, released under CC0 1.0. For reproducibility, Drift\nvendors exact files from a pinned revision of the public\n`Daarko/sparkstream-sounds` mirror.\n\n`scripts/vendor-sonic-assets.py` verifies each downloaded file against its\nexpected Git blob SHA-1, verifies RIFF/WAVE headers, computes SHA-256, preserves\nthe pack licence texts, and writes `src/sonic/assets/manifest.json`.\n\nThe manifest records the local path, exact upstream revision and path, Git blob\nhash, SHA-256, byte length, source pack, physical material, intended use,\ncanonical Kenney page, and licence identifier.\n\n## Tuning boundaries\n\n- Master, passages, controls, density, variation, and under-voice gain are\n  normalized from 0 to 1.\n- Motion cues cannot exceed the master and motion-family gains.\n- Passage density is quantized to every first, second, or third crossing rather\n  than becoming frame-rate-dependent.\n- Cues within 45 ms of a seamless loop boundary are omitted to prevent a\n  doubled seam.\n- Reduced-motion output is silent.\n- Vertical motion remains centred; horizontal motion uses restrained pan.\n- No cue is scheduled by `setTimeout()` in exported audio.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- music selection or playback;\n- long ambience, room tone, projectors, or film-reel loops;\n- generated or synthesized sound effects;\n- user-uploaded sample libraries;\n- a DAW-style timeline;\n- automatic loudness mastering;\n- sound on hover, every drag pixel, or every range-input event.\n')
write("docs/SONIC_GAUNTLET.md", '# Sonic gauntlet\n\nThis checklist is the review contract for the tactile sound branch. A green\nbuild is necessary but not sufficient.\n\n## Journey 1 — first open\n\n- The project opens with no browser autoplay warning.\n- The interface explains that the vocabulary is foley, not music.\n- Preview sound only arms after a trusted gesture.\n- Exported effects are visibly off by default.\n- Audition is explicit and works without starting carousel playback.\n- Muting preview does not change MP4 inclusion.\n- Enabling MP4 inclusion does not force preview sound on.\n\n## Journey 2 — shaping the carousel\n\n- A passage cue occurs once per logical threshold, not once per rendered frame.\n- Fast motion is density-limited rather than machine-gunned.\n- Dragging emits one grab and one release, not a continuous loop.\n- Slider movement is silent; it does not chatter on every input event.\n- Variation changes both sample choice and restrained playback rate.\n- Variation zero is stable and repeatable.\n- Horizontal direction affects pan; vertical motion remains centred.\n- Pausing, focus mode, theme changes, and discrete controls remain restrained.\n\n## Journey 3 — narration\n\n- Presenter speech remains intelligible at every built-in palette.\n- Under-voice gain applies only when sound and presenter audio coexist.\n- Muting presenter audio cannot accidentally mute authored effects.\n- Disabling authored effects cannot remove presenter speech.\n- The MP4 contains exactly one audio track.\n\n## Journey 4 — export\n\n- Picture and sound use the exact encoded duration, not nominal UI duration.\n- 24, 25, and 30 fps sound-bearing exports pass codec and decode readback.\n- 50/60 fps fails visibly while audio is enabled.\n- Sound-only output is valid AAC, not a silent placeholder track.\n- Mixed output is sample-aligned and clipped safely.\n- Cancellation cannot leave preview muted or resources retained.\n- A failed export restores preview suppression and reports the real failure.\n- Repeated exports do not accumulate AudioContexts, nodes, or timers.\n\n## Journey 5 — reopen and migration\n\n- Every sound control persists in the local project.\n- Applying a visual theme preserves sound direction.\n- Schema-v1 projects migrate without surprise audio: preview off, export off.\n- A migrated user can opt in through the same controls as a new project.\n- Corrupt or missing sound state fails validation rather than being guessed.\n\n## Accessibility and privacy\n\n- Sound is never the sole carrier of status.\n- Every sound control is keyboard accessible and labelled.\n- Reduced-motion output is silent.\n- Hidden tabs suspend preview audio.\n- No sound file is requested from a third-party origin at runtime.\n- Offline export works from committed assets.\n\n## Asset integrity\n\n- Every committed recording has a RIFF/WAVE header.\n- Every recording matches the pinned upstream Git blob SHA-1.\n- Every manifest SHA-256 and byte length matches the committed file.\n- Every source pack has a local CC0 licence text.\n- No generated UI bleeps or Freesound preview files remain.\n- The catalogue imports only committed local recordings.\n\n## Required automated gates\n\n- TypeScript typecheck.\n- Unit tests for deterministic planning, density, seam handling, panning,\n  migration, PCM mixing, and asset integrity.\n- Production build.\n- Chromium end-to-end persistence test with zero external requests.\n- Chromium sound-design-only MP4 test with verified AAC readback.\n- Existing repository CI with no unrelated regression.\n')
write("ASSET-LICENSE.md", '# Asset licence\n\nOriginal demo slide artwork generated by `src/lib/demoSlides.ts`, the synthetic\ntest fixtures at `e2e/fixtures/slide.png`, `e2e/fixtures/audio-only.mp4`, and\n`e2e/fixtures/presenter.mp4`, and the repository screenshot at\n`docs/media/drift-studio.png` are licensed under the\n[Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).\n\nAttribution: **Drift demo artwork and test fixtures by pitch.dog, 2026 —\nCC BY-SA 4.0.**\n\n## Tactile foley recordings\n\nDrift includes selected recordings from Kenney\'s\n[Casino Audio](https://kenney.nl/assets/casino-audio),\n[RPG Audio](https://kenney.nl/assets/rpg-audio), and\n[Impact Sounds](https://kenney.nl/assets/impact-sounds) packs. Kenney releases\nthese packs under **CC0 1.0 Universal**.\n\nFor reproducible vendoring, the exact files are retrieved from\n`Daarko/sparkstream-sounds` at pinned revision\n`a7a3ee178d2ec48f4354782f244ab777a0e238df`. This mirror is a transport and\nprovenance boundary; the canonical source pages remain Kenney.\n\n- Exact local and upstream paths, Git blob SHA-1 values, SHA-256 values, byte\n  lengths, source packs, materials, and intended uses are recorded in\n  `src/sonic/assets/manifest.json`.\n- Original pack licence texts are preserved under\n  `src/sonic/assets/licenses/`.\n- `scripts/vendor-sonic-assets.py --verify` checks the committed corpus without\n  contacting the network.\n- Production preview and export make no third-party sound request.\n\nCC0 does not require attribution. Drift retains this notice because exact\nprovenance is a product-quality and supply-chain requirement.\n\nUser-imported decks, images, presenter videos, project bundles, and rendered\noutputs are not repository assets and are not relicensed. They remain the\nproperty of their owners.\n\nThe pitch.dog name and marks are addressed separately in\n[TRADEMARKS.md](TRADEMARKS.md).\n')
write("THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md", '# Third-party notices\n\nDrift’s source licence does not replace dependency or asset licences. Exact\npackage versions and transitive packages are locked in `package-lock.json`;\nexact sound-file provenance is locked in `src/sonic/assets/manifest.json`.\n\n| Dependency / asset | Version | Licence | Role |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| React / React DOM | 19.2.8 | MIT | Interface |\n| Three.js | 0.185.1 | MIT | WebGL scene and resources |\n| Mediabunny | 1.55.1 | MPL-2.0 | Media decode, encode, mux, and readback |\n| @mediabunny/aac-encoder | 1.55.1 | MPL-2.0 | Software AAC encoder extension |\n| FFmpeg `libavcodec` / `libavutil` | Embedded in the AAC extension’s WASM | LGPL-2.1-or-later under the extension’s published non-GPL configure flags | AAC encoding implementation |\n| fflate | 0.8.3 | MIT | Portable project and PNG-sequence ZIPs |\n| Kenney Casino Audio | pinned files | CC0-1.0 | Card slides, placements, and shoves |\n| Kenney RPG Audio | pinned files | CC0-1.0 | Paper, cloth, leather, book, and metal foley |\n| Kenney Impact Sounds | pinned files | CC0-1.0 | Restrained soft, hard, and wood impacts |\n\nThe Kenney files are transported from `Daarko/sparkstream-sounds` at exact\nrevision `a7a3ee178d2ec48f4354782f244ab777a0e238df`. Canonical source pages,\nlicence copies, hashes, and per-file purposes are preserved with the assets.\n\nDevelopment tooling includes TypeScript, Vite, Vitest, Playwright, Python, and\nReact type packages under their respective upstream licences.\n\nNo third-party font, stock photograph, presenter clip, proprietary shader,\nmusic track, generated UI sound, or remote runtime sound is bundled.\n\n## AAC / FFmpeg distribution boundary\n\n`@mediabunny/aac-encoder` states that it embeds a size-optimised FFmpeg AAC\nencoder compiled to WASM. FFmpeg’s\n[official legal guidance](https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html) identifies its default\nterms as LGPL-2.1-or-later and requires a distributor to provide the exact\ncorresponding source and build provenance for the binary it ships.\n\nThis GitHub project publishes source and a package lock only. `node_modules/`,\nVite `dist/`, and rendered application bundles are excluded. No hosted or\ndownloadable compiled build is released from this repository yet.\n\nBefore distributing a compiled Drift build, a maintainer must record the exact\nFFmpeg source revision, configure command, patches, and relink materials used\nby the embedded WASM; provide the corresponding source and LGPL text alongside\nthat build; and satisfy the current FFmpeg compliance checklist. Until that\nevidence exists, the verified publication scope is the source repository and\nlocal builds—not a binary release or hosted deployment.\n')
write("tests/sonicAssets.test.ts", 'import { createHash } from "node:crypto";\nimport { readFileSync } from "node:fs";\nimport { resolve } from "node:path";\nimport { describe, expect, it } from "vitest";\n\ninterface ManifestRecording {\n  localPath: string;\n  upstreamRevision: string;\n  gitBlobSha1: string;\n  sha256: string;\n  bytes: number;\n  license: string;\n  canonicalSource: string;\n}\n\ninterface SonicManifest {\n  upstreamRevision: string;\n  runtimeNetworkRequests: boolean;\n  recordings: ManifestRecording[];\n  licenseFiles: Array<{\n    localPath: string;\n    license: string;\n  }>;\n}\n\nfunction gitBlobSha1(data: Buffer): string {\n  const header = Buffer.from(`blob ${data.length}\\0`, "ascii");\n  return createHash("sha1").update(header).update(data).digest("hex");\n}\n\ndescribe("authentic tactile asset ledger", () => {\n  const manifestPath = resolve(\n    process.cwd(),\n    "src/sonic/assets/manifest.json",\n  );\n  const manifest = JSON.parse(\n    readFileSync(manifestPath, "utf8"),\n  ) as SonicManifest;\n\n  it("pins a local CC0 corpus with no runtime request path", () => {\n    expect(manifest.upstreamRevision).toBe(\n      "a7a3ee178d2ec48f4354782f244ab777a0e238df",\n    );\n    expect(manifest.runtimeNetworkRequests).toBe(false);\n    expect(manifest.recordings.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(20);\n    expect(manifest.licenseFiles).toHaveLength(3);\n  });\n\n  it("verifies every WAV header, byte length and cryptographic digest", () => {\n    for (const entry of manifest.recordings) {\n      const data = readFileSync(resolve(process.cwd(), entry.localPath));\n      expect(data.subarray(0, 4).toString("ascii")).toBe("RIFF");\n      expect(data.subarray(8, 12).toString("ascii")).toBe("WAVE");\n      expect(data.length).toBe(entry.bytes);\n      expect(gitBlobSha1(data)).toBe(entry.gitBlobSha1);\n      expect(createHash("sha256").update(data).digest("hex")).toBe(\n        entry.sha256,\n      );\n      expect(entry.upstreamRevision).toBe(manifest.upstreamRevision);\n      expect(entry.license).toBe("CC0-1.0");\n      expect(entry.canonicalSource).toMatch(/^https:\\/\\/kenney\\.nl\\/assets\\//);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it("preserves the original CC0 notice for each source pack", () => {\n    for (const entry of manifest.licenseFiles) {\n      const text = readFileSync(\n        resolve(process.cwd(), entry.localPath),\n        "utf8",\n      );\n      expect(entry.license).toBe("CC0-1.0");\n      expect(text.toUpperCase()).toContain("CC0");\n    }\n  });\n});\n')

